questions.explanation:
**Given:**

(1 - sec&sup2;&theta;)(1 - sin&theta;)(1 + sin&theta;)(1 + cot&sup2;&theta;)

**Formula Used:**

sec&sup2;&theta; - 1 = tan&sup2;&theta;

cot&sup2;&theta; + 1 = cosec&sup2;&theta;

**Calculation:**

(1 - sec&sup2;&theta;) = -tan&sup2;&theta;

(1 - sin&theta;)(1 + sin&theta;) = 1 - sin&sup2;&theta; = cos&sup2;&theta;

(1 + cot&sup2;&theta;) = cosec&sup2;&theta;

Substituting these values:

(- tan&sup2;&theta;) × (cos&sup2;&theta;) × (cosec&sup2;&theta;)

Since tan&theta; = sin&theta; / cos&theta; and cosec&theta; = 1 / sin&theta;:

- (sin&sup2;&theta; / cos&sup2;&theta;) × cos&sup2;&theta; × (1 / sin&sup2;&theta;)

Canceling sin&sup2;&theta; and cos&sup2;&theta;:

-1

**&there4; Option 2 is the correct answer.**

